TEST 38477 -- ATMF - Virtual link
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-09-21, tb470
DUT:    IE520 4-member VCStack, AMF node "IE520-stk"
Peer:   AR4050S-5G, AMF node "4050-5g" (AMF master at this point)
L3 path: vlan10 10.10.10.0/27 -- stack .1, 4050 .2, static routes each way,
         carried over po1. This path already existed on the bench.

VERDICT: PASS

STEP -- "Check DUT can join an AMF network using a virtual link"

  1. NEGATIVE CONTROL FIRST. The L2 AMF path was removed entirely on both ends
     (no switchport atmf-crosslink; po1 returned to plain access vlan 10) so
     that no layer-2 ATMF adjacency could exist.
       before teardown : ATMF nodes = 2 on both
       after  teardown : ATMF nodes = 1 on BOTH nodes   <-- network gone
       IP reachability : ping 10.10.10.2 -> 3 packets transmitted, 3 received,
                         0% packet loss                 <-- L3 path intact
     This control is what makes the rest of the case meaningful: anything that
     rejoins from here can ONLY be joining over the virtual link.

  2. Virtual links configured:
       DUT   : atmf virtual-link id 1 ip 10.10.10.1 remote-id 2 remote-ip 10.10.10.2
       Peer  : atmf virtual-link id 2 ip 10.10.10.2 remote-id 1 remote-ip 10.10.10.1
     Both accepted with no error.

  3. Result -- ATMF nodes returned to 2 on both, with no L2 ATMF path present.

     show atmf virtual-links (on 4050-5g):
       Local   Local              Remote              Tunnel   Tunnel
       Port    ID   IP            ID   IP             Protect  State
       vlink2  2    10.10.10.2    1    10.10.10.1     -        Complete
       Virtual Links Configured: 1

  PASS -- the DUT joined the AMF network over a virtual link, with the tunnel
  reported "Complete" and the layer-2 ATMF path proven absent beforehand.

